{"1-9":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"bath-rabbim-h1337","name":"Bath-rabbim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"heshbon-h2809","name":"Heshbon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"lebanon-h3844g","name":"Lebanon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"carmel-h3760g","name":"Carmel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"words":[{"base":"H7699","lemma":"שַׁד","tr":"shad","gloss":"breast","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":24},{"base":"H1337","lemma":"בַּת־רַבִּים","tr":"bat rab·bim","gloss":"Bath-rabbim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3302","lemma":"יָפָה","tr":"ya·phah","gloss":"be beautiful","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H8558","lemma":"תָּמָר","tr":"ta·mar","gloss":"palm","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H0811","lemma":"אֶשְׁכּוֹל","tr":"esh·kol","gloss":"cluster","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H4026","lemma":"מִגְדָּל","tr":"mig·dal","gloss":"(Hananel) Tower","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":48},{"base":"H4100","lemma":"מָה","tr":"mah","gloss":"what?","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":752},{"base":"H0639","lemma":"אַף","tr":"aph","gloss":"face: anger","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":276},{"base":"H2481","lemma":"חֲלִי","tr":"cha·li","gloss":"ornament","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6646","lemma":"צְבִיָּה","tr":"tse·viy·yah","gloss":"gazelle","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":45,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"and the king will desire your beauty; bow to him, for he is your lord.","from":6},{"book":"SNG","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"How beautiful you are, my darling! Oh, how very beautiful! Your eyes are like doves.","from":6},{"book":"SNG","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"How handsome you are, my beloved! Oh, how delightful! The soft grass is our bed.","from":6},{"book":"SNG","chapter":4,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"How delightful is your love, my sister, my bride! Your love is much better than wine, and the fragrance of your perfume than all spices.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":45,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"All glorious is the princess in her chamber; her gown is embroidered with gold.","from":1},{"book":"SNG","chapter":2,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"O my dove in the clefts of the rock, in the crevices of the cliff, let me see your face, let me hear your voice; for your voice is sweet, and your countenance is lovely.","from":6},{"book":"SNG","chapter":4,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Your neck is like the tower of David, built with rows of stones; on it hang a thousand shields, all of them shields of warriors.","from":4},{"book":"SNG","chapter":4,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Your breasts are like two fawns, twins of a gazelle grazing among the lilies.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"10-13":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1730","lemma":"דּוֹד","tr":"dod","gloss":"beloved","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":61},{"base":"H9032","lemma":"ךְ","tr":"kh","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":333},{"base":"H3723","lemma":"כָּפָר","tr":"ka·phar","gloss":"Chephar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5132","lemma":"נָצָה","tr":"na·tsah","gloss":"to flee","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5563","lemma":"סְמַדֵר","tr":"se·ma·dar","gloss":"blossom","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H8669","lemma":"תְּשׁוּקָה","tr":"te·shu·qah","gloss":"desire","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H1736","lemma":"דּוּדַי","tr":"du·day","gloss":"mandrake","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H3465","lemma":"יָשָׁן","tr":"ya·shan","gloss":"(Gate of) Yeshanah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4022","lemma":"מֶ֫גֶד","tr":"me·ged","gloss":"excellence","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H6845","lemma":"צָפַן","tr":"tsa·phan","gloss":"to treasure","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":32}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":45,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"and the king will desire your beauty; bow to him, for he is your lord.","from":10},{"book":"SNG","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"My beloved is mine and I am his; he pastures his flock among the lilies.","from":10},{"book":"SNG","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I belong to my beloved and he belongs to me; he pastures his flock among the lilies.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now during the wheat harvest, Reuben went out and found some mandrakes in the field. When he brought them to his mother, Rachel begged Leah, “Please give me some of your sonʼs mandrakes.”","from":13},{"book":"SNG","chapter":6,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I went down to the walnut grove to see the blossoms of the valley, to see if the vines were budding or the pomegranates were in bloom.","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":25,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And I will meet with you there above the mercy seat, between the two cherubim that are over the ark of the Testimony; I will speak with you about all that I command you regarding the Israelites.","from":12},{"book":"JOB","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You will call, and I will answer; You will desire the work of Your hands.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":43,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then I will go to the altar of God, to God, my greatest joy. I will praise You with the harp, O God, my God.","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}